[i]Paste this into the Workshop item's description field on the website.
WorkshopTool ignores name and description on update unless -namedesc up is
passed, so what you paste there survives every release. Keep it in step with
release/RELEASE_NOTES.md by hand; the two audiences read the same text.[/i]

I never liked the vanilla gunnery control chair - you sit down and get the same
boring menu. This mod replaces it with a real turret console.

[h2]New in this release[/h2]

[b]Bug fixes[/b]
[list]
[*]Direct-control now works on M ships that resolve camera view to the ship
container instead of a dedicated turret camera.
[*]If a target-view camera attach fails, target selection stays open instead of
kicking you out of the session.
[*]Turret groups with duplicate names are now still controllable.
[*]The group [b]Mode[/b] column now refreshes correctly after
[b]Cease Engagement[/b].
[/list]

[h2]What you can do[/h2]

[b]Pick your turret groups.[/b] Every physical turret group gets a row with a
checkbox. Check the ones you want, or use [b]Select all[/b]. Names read like
[i]Front Upper Left[/i], with the turret type when the game exposes it. You can
set each group's [b]Mode[/b] and [b]Armed[/b] state right there, same as on the
ship's behaviour tab.

Then two buttons light up:

[b]Auto-engage[/b] - issues no fire orders. Your turrets still choose their own
targets, but before entering the camera it writes your checked groups' staged
console settings to the ship (so ticking a group, which sets its Mode to
[b]Attack all enemies[/b], does take effect for the duration). The camera cycles
only through the turrets of the checked groups. Everything is reverted when you
press [b]Get Up[/b].

[b]Direct-control[/b] - you tell the checked groups what to shoot.
[b]Select Engagement Target[/b] lists ships and stations in radar range; click
one and its hull is engaged immediately. You can also point every checked group
at a specific surface element instead - a turret, a shield generator, an engine.

In Direct-control, your checked groups focus your chosen target. If that target
is out of range for some checked turrets, those turrets can sit idle until it
comes back in range or you pick another target.

[list]
[*][b]Auto-next Target when destroyed[/b] is on by default: when the target
dies, everything moves to the next one automatically. Turn it off and the mod
stops and asks you to pick the next target yourself, which feels a lot more like
actually manning the gun.
[*][b]Next Target[/b] / [b]Previous Target[/b] step through the same list
without reopening the browser.
[/list]

Ticking a group's checkbox sets that group's Mode to [b]Attack all enemies[/b].
Everything you change in the console is temporary and undone when you press
[b]Get Up[/b] - unless you press [b]Update turret behavior[/b] first, which
makes the changes permanent.

[h2]Four ways to watch[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Turret POV manual[/b] / [b]Target POV manual[/b] - camera on the turret,
or on what it is shooting at, with the normal UI still up. Hold Shift + middle
mouse button to look around.
[*][b]Turret POV cinematic[/b] / [b]Target POV cinematic[/b] - the same two
viewpoints through the game's cutscene camera, which hides all UI and aims for
you. Esc returns you to the manual panel.
[*][b]Next Turret[/b] / [b]Previous Turret[/b] cycle the camera through every
operational turret in the checked groups. This only moves the camera; it never
changes what is being shot at.
[/list]

[h2]Leaving the seat[/h2]

[b]Get Up[/b], closing the console, undocking, or changing ships puts every
group back to whatever you last made permanent with [b]Update turret behavior[/b],
and a short popup confirms it.

[h2]Things to know[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]This is not manual aiming.[/b] X4 still decides barrel traverse, lead,
when to fire, and whether a target is legal to attack. You say [i]what[/i], not
[i]how[/i].
[*][b]Turret POV cinematic often clips into your own hull[/b] and looks rough.
Target POV cinematic is the prettier of the two.
[*]On some S/M ships, turret target view can resolve to a wider ship-level
camera framing instead of a tight turret component view.
[*]If two turret groups share the same name, some member rows or camera picks
can appear under the sibling label. Commands still apply to the correct group.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]

[list]
[*]X4 Foundations 9.00 or newer.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3477279743]kuertee
UI Extensions and HUD[/url] 9.00 or newer. This is a hard requirement - X4 will
not load Gunnery Control without it. Steam lists it as a required item and
subscribes you to it along with this mod.
[/list]

